13. Interview Questions
=======================

Q1. What are variadic templates?

Templates that accept zero or more template arguments.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q2. When were variadic templates introduced?

C++11

---------------------------------------------------------

Q3. What problem do they solve?

They eliminate the need for multiple overloaded functions that differ only
in the number of arguments.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q4. What is a parameter pack?

A collection of template arguments.

Example

template<typename... Args>

---------------------------------------------------------

Q5. What is parameter pack expansion?

Expanding the parameter pack using

args...

Example

print(args...);

---------------------------------------------------------

Q6. What does sizeof...(Args) return?

The number of template arguments.

Example

sizeof...(Args)

---------------------------------------------------------

Q7. Why is a base case required in recursive variadic templates?

To stop the recursion once all arguments have been processed.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q8. What are fold expressions?

A C++17 feature that applies an operator to all elements in a parameter pack,
eliminating the need for recursion.

Example

(... + args)

---------------------------------------------------------

Q9. Difference between recursive variadic templates and fold expressions?

Recursive Variadic Templates

• Introduced in C++11

• Require a base case

• More code

--------------------------------------

Fold Expressions

• Introduced in C++17

• No recursion

• Simpler and more efficient

---------------------------------------------------------

Q10. Where are variadic templates used in STL?

• std::make_shared()

• std::make_unique()

• std::thread

• vector::emplace_back()

